        "original_id": "9b8e7580-b7a6-5999-a9bd-790188724051",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Romance of the Far Fur Country\n- Companies: Hudson's Bay Company\n- Topics: Arctic fur trappers, fur trade, retail operations\n\nFacts:\n- The Romance of the Far Fur Country is a historical documentary film about Arctic fur trappers in 1919.\n- The Romance of the Far Fur Country was made to commemorate the 250th anniversary of the Hudson's Bay Company in 1920.\n- Hudson's Bay Company was a fur trading business for much of its history.\n- Hudson's Bay Company owns and operates retail stores in Canada, Belgium, Germany, the Netherlands, and the United States.\n- Hudson's Bay Company's retail operations include Galeria Kaufhof, Gilt, Hudson's Bay, Home Outfitters, Lord & Taylor, and Saks Fifth Avenue.",
